---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const SIM_URL = 'https://sim.failurefirst.ai/?preset=evidence';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="SimLab — Failure-First Embodied AI"
  description="Watch recorded embodied-AI failures, follow the causal chain, inspect falsifiers, and reach the hash-addressed source trace. SimLab is Failure-First's evidence theatre."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'SimLab' }]}
  animation="signal"
  accent="cyan"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">WATCH &rarr; EXPLAIN &rarr; FALSIFY &rarr; RECEIPT</p>
    <h1>See what the trace actually proves.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The current Real Evidence preset is a measured Go2 stand-up control: the
      body starts prone, the apparatus records the transition, and a phase-scoped
      falsifier checks body-height drop. No model contacted this run. SimLab says
      that plainly instead of inventing cognition, sensors, peer messages, or a
      failure story the trace does not contain.
    </p>
    <a class="cta" href={SIM_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Watch what happened <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
    <p class="receipt-note">Open the forensic console in the replay to inspect the run identity, phase-scoped falsifier, unavailable channels, and source-trace hash.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>1. Watch what happened</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Real Evidence</strong> preset replays a genuine MuJoCo control
        trace in temporal order. Watch the robot move from prone to standing and
        inspect the recorded body state. There is no model-decision event in this run.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>2. Why we think it happened</h2>
      <p>
        The forensic console can keep world observation, model/tool contact, peer
        transmission, policy decision, actuator state, and outcome in one chain
        when a recording carries them. Here, missing channels say
        <code>UNAVAILABLE</code>. Declared state never silently substitutes for physical state.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>3. What would falsify it</h2>
      <p>
        Verdicts name the check, phase, and denominator they actually cover. A
        phase-scoped result never becomes a whole-scenario claim. Failed recovery,
        hard nulls, missing causal contact, and controls remain visible.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>4. Inspect the receipt</h2>
      <p>
        Every production replay derives from a finalized, hash-addressed recording.
        Deterministic deep links preserve preset, time, and playback state so another
        reader can reopen the same joint in the causal chain.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>UTOPIA / DYSTOPIA</h2>
      <p>
        A presentation-only world switch: the same recorded evidence renders as a
        bright robotics-institute laboratory or a dark industrial one. Camera
        geometry, timestamps, and verdicts are provably unaffected &mdash; only
        pixels change.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Built for scrutiny</h2>
      <p>
        Deterministic deep links (<code>?preset=&hellip;&amp;t=&hellip;&amp;paused</code>),
        strict schema validation on every recording, and official Unitree
        URDF/mesh assets pinned to an exact upstream commit with a SHA-256
        manifest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="footnote">
    Source: <code>apps/simviz/</code> in the research repository. Rendering is
    <code>DERIVED_VISUALISATION</code> &mdash; it never alters or implies
    changes to a recorded trajectory.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--fg-muted, #7a8292);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg, #e8ecf2);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
    margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
  }
  .cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background: var(--accent-primary, #00d2ff);
    color: #050810;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-bottom: none;
    transition: transform 150ms ease, box-shadow 150ms ease;
  }
  .cta:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 210, 255, 0.25);
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .card {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(232, 236, 242, 0.08));
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--bg-card, #0f1621);
  }
  .card h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--fg, #e8ecf2);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .card code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #00d2ff);
  }

  .footnote {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--fg-muted, #7a8292);
    text-align: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle, rgba(232, 236, 242, 0.08));
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  .footnote code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    color: var(--fg-dim, #b0b8c5);
  }
</style>
